<SanitizeModelResponse name="SMR-SanitizeModelResponse" continueOnError="true" enabled="true">
  <DisplayName>Sanitize Model Response (Model Armor)</DisplayName>
  <!--
    continueOnError="true" since 2026-09-15, same decision and same caveats as
    SUP-SanitizeUserPrompt — see that file's comment for the full reasoning.
    RF-ResponseBlocked is the compensating control that keeps a genuine match
    enforced; this attribute and that policy must move together.

    Worth stating for the response side specifically: failing open here means a
    model response reaches the caller unscanned. The prompt was still scanned
    (or recorded as unscanned) on the way in, so this is the narrower exposure
    of the two, but it is the one that can surface unsafe generated content
    directly to a user. ma_response_failed in the attribution log is the only
    signal it happened.
  -->
  <Source>response</Source>
  <!--
    Explicit for the same reason as SUP-SanitizeUserPrompt: the policy default
    uses negative array indices, which Apigee's message-template jsonPath()
    resolves to an empty string, and an empty prompt/response is a FATAL
    "Template was resolved to empty string" rather than a skipped scan.
    Note also the path must be UNQUOTED; quoting it fails the same way, which
    cost a deploy cycle to learn. Vertex generateContent responses are shaped
    {"candidates":[{"content":{"parts":[{"text": "..."}]}}],"usageMetadata":{}}.
  -->
  <LLMResponseSource>{llm.response_text}</LLMResponseSource>
  <ModelArmor>
    <!--
      Template is INSPECT-only by configuration (no SDP advanced_config /
      deidentify_template — see the long comment in
      terraform/7-apigee-runtime/model-armor.tf). That matters specifically
      here: a template that rewrites the response body can strip
      groundingMetadata.groundingChunks and searchEntryPoint from a
      Google-Search-grounded Gemini response without erroring, which
      Sales-Agent's search agent reads to build its evidence list. The symptom
      would be zero evidence on an HTTP 200 — no error anywhere.
    -->
    <TemplateName>projects/gclt-aicoe-dev-llm/locations/europe-west3/templates/aicoe-llm-gateway</TemplateName>
  </ModelArmor>
</SanitizeModelResponse>
